{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794130896,"nonce":"7cfUBsVLvhq5WvKJgEgJHRaoPes=","message":"Done in the working tree, not committed. The stack travels as one comma-joined family string, so every public signature that takes font_name is unchanged. parse_font_family keeps the named families in order up to the first generic keyword (the keyword ends the list, as in CSS; system-ui first now means no named family). FontRegistry::resolve_styled splits the stack (family_stack) and uses the first family installed, cached or loadable, before the generic. Measure cache keys and the glyph-atlas font id already hash the whole string. Tests: parser (order, quotes, generic ends list), registry (missing first family falls to the next installed; an installed first beats a cached later one), measurer (a stack is measured in Fira Code when the first family is missing), red when the split is disabled; green on macOS and on the Ubuntu NUC; nextest on css, text, layout, theme, cn, core and the recorder suite. Limits: a family whose name contains a comma cannot be named; per-glyph fallback along the stack (browsers try the next family for a missing glyph) is not done, the existing script fallbacks (CJK, emoji) still apply.","files":null}]}